- `resolveRepoClusterHost`'s owner/repo branch collects distinct active mirror cluster hosts and refuses (returns ok=false) whenever there's more than one — i.e. every multi-homed repo. Its caller, `resolveRepoCellTarget`, then returns `nil`, and callers fall back to **home-jurisdiction routing** — which silently reads the wrong region's data for `entire trail` and `entire experts` on any multi-homed repo. This is a live, verified bug (confirmed against prod): `entire trail list --repo gh/entirehq/entire.io` should list real trails on cell `aws-us-east-2` but instead falls back and reports "No open trails found."
